    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Australian Statistician to have functions etc. of Commonwealth",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf, p.6",
      "values:originalText": "Statistician\n\n(2) After the commencement of this Act:\n\n(a) the Australian Statistician shall:\n\n(i) have the functions, powers and duties expressed by any\nAct, or by any regulations or other instrument made\nunder any Act, to be conferred or imposed on the\nCommonwealth Statistician; and\n\n(ii) have the functions and powers expressed by a law of a\nTerritory, or by any regulations or other instrument\nmade under such a law, to be conferred on the\nCommonwealth Statistician; and\n\n(b) a reference in any Act, in any law of a Territory, or in an\ninstrument under any Act or law of a Territory, to the\nCommonwealth Statistician shall have effect as if the office\nof Australian Statistician were a continuation of the office of\nthe Commonwealth Statistician.\n\n\nAustralian Bureau of Statistics and Australian Statistician  Part II\n\nSection 5\n\nAustralian Bureau of Statistics Act 1975\nCompilation date: 3/5/19\nRegistered: 10/5/19",
      "skos:definition": "Statistician\n\n(2) After the commencement of this Act:\n\n(a) the Australian Statistician shall:\n\n(i) have the functions, powers and duties expressed by any\nAct, or by any regulations or other instrument made\nunder any Act, to be conferred or imposed on the\nCommonwealth Statistician; and\n\n(ii) have the functions and powers expressed by a law of a\nTerritory, or by any regulations or other instrument\nmade under such a law, to be conferred on the\nCommonwealth Statistician; and\n\n(b) a reference in any Act, in any law of a Territory, or in an\ninstrument under any Act or law of a Territory, to the\nCommonwealth Statistician shall have effect as if the office\nof Australian Statistician were a continuation of the office of\nthe Commonwealth Statistician.\n\n\nAustralian Bureau of Statistics and Australian Statistician  Part II\n\nSection 5\n\nAustralian Bureau of Statistics Act 1975\nCompilation date: 3/5/19\nRegistered: 10/5/19",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f812b68a3f5c7b431f8817c39ea14ea1390027d6d4b60720678b2694c786f162",
      "skos:note": "Functions and powers of Australian Statistician"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Australian Statistician to have functions etc. of Commonwealth",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 6,
      "values:originalText": "Statistician\n\n(2) After the commencement of this Act:\n\n(a) the Australian Statistician shall:\n\n(i) have the functions, powers and duties expressed by any\nAct, or by any regulations or other instrument made\nunder any Act, to be conferred or imposed on the\nCommonwealth Statistician; and\n\n(ii) have the functions and powers expressed by a law of a\nTerritory, or by any regulations or other instrument\nmade under such a law, to be conferred on the\nCommonwealth Statistician; and\n\n(b) a reference in any Act, in any law of a Territory, or in an\ninstrument under any Act or law of a Territory, to the\nCommonwealth Statistician shall have effect as if the office\nof Australian Statistician were a continuation of the office of\nthe Commonwealth Statistician.\n\n\nAustralian Bureau of Statistics and Australian Statistician  Part II\n\nSection 5\n\nAustralian Bureau of Statistics Act 1975\nCompilation date: 3/5/19\nRegistered: 10/5/19"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5 Establishment of Bureau and office of Statistician",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(1) There is hereby established a Bureau to be known as the Australian\nBureau of Statistics.\n\n(2) There shall be an Australian Statistician.\n\n(3) The Bureau shall consist of the Statistician and the staff referred to\nin subsection 16(1).\n\n(4) The Statistician shall control the operations of the Bureau and shall\nhave such other functions, powers and duties as are conferred or\nimposed upon the Statistician by or under any Act and such other\nfunctions and powers as are conferred upon the Statistician by or\nunder any law of a Territory.\n\n(5) For the purposes of the finance law (within the meaning of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013):\n\n(a) the Bureau is a listed entity; and\n\n(b) the Statistician is the accountable authority of the Bureau;\nand\n\n(c) the following persons are officials of the Bureau:\n\n(i) the Statistician;\n\n(ii) the staff referred to in subsection 16(1);\n\n(iii) persons engaged under subsection 16(2); and\n\n(d) the purposes of the Bureau include:\n\n(i) the functions of the Bureau referred to in section 6; and\n\n(ii) the functions of the Statistician referred to in\nsubsection (4) and section 4.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) There is hereby established a Bureau to be known as the Australian\nBureau of Statistics.\n\n(2) There shall be an Australian Statistician.\n\n(3) The Bureau shall consist of the Statistician and the staff referred to\nin subsection 16(1).\n\n(4) The Statistician shall control the operations of the Bureau and shall\nhave such other functions, powers and duties as are conferred or\nimposed upon the Statistician by or under any Act and such other\nfunctions and powers as are conferred upon the Statistician by or\nunder any law of a Territory.\n\n(5) For the purposes of the finance law (within the meaning of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013):\n\n(a) the Bureau is a listed entity; and\n\n(b) the Statistician is the accountable authority of the Bureau;\nand\n\n(c) the following persons are officials of the Bureau:\n\n(i) the Statistician;\n\n(ii) the staff referred to in subsection 16(1);\n\n(iii) persons engaged under subsection 16(2); and\n\n(d) the purposes of the Bureau include:\n\n(i) the functions of the Bureau referred to in section 6; and\n\n(ii) the functions of the Statistician referred to in\nsubsection (4) and section 4.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-5-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-5-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-5-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-5-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-5-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "64161c6b406039f65f273a9703766b1ecafa42076f68319419a6052248e161d1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 Establishment of Bureau and office of Statistician",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(1) There is hereby established a Bureau to be known as the Australian\nBureau of Statistics.\n\n(2) There shall be an Australian Statistician.\n\n(3) The Bureau shall consist of the Statistician and the staff referred to\nin subsection 16(1).\n\n(4) The Statistician shall control the operations of the Bureau and shall\nhave such other functions, powers and duties as are conferred or\nimposed upon the Statistician by or under any Act and such other\nfunctions and powers as are conferred upon the Statistician by or\nunder any law of a Territory.\n\n(5) For the purposes of the finance law (within the meaning of the\nPublic Governance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013):\n\n(a) the Bureau is a listed entity; and\n\n(b) the Statistician is the accountable authority of the Bureau;\nand\n\n(c) the following persons are officials of the Bureau:\n\n(i) the Statistician;\n\n(ii) the staff referred to in subsection 16(1);\n\n(iii) persons engaged under subsection 16(2); and\n\n(d) the purposes of the Bureau include:\n\n(i) the functions of the Bureau referred to in section 6; and\n\n(ii) the functions of the Statistician referred to in\nsubsection (4) and section 4."
    },
