    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(4) Functions of Bureau",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-6-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where, in relation to a proposal to which subsection (3) is\napplicable, being a proposal for the collection of information\nrelating to businesses, the Minister considers it necessary to\ncommence implementation of the proposal at a time when it is not\npracticable to comply with subsection (3) the Minister may\nauthorize the implementation of the proposal without compliance\nwith that subsection but in such a case particulars of the nature of\nthe information to which the authorization relates shall be laid\nbefore each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days of that\nHouse after the giving of the authorization.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where, in relation to a proposal to which subsection (3) is\napplicable, being a proposal for the collection of information\nrelating to businesses, the Minister considers it necessary to\ncommence implementation of the proposal at a time when it is not\npracticable to comply with subsection (3) the Minister may\nauthorize the implementation of the proposal without compliance\nwith that subsection but in such a case particulars of the nature of\nthe information to which the authorization relates shall be laid\nbefore each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days of that\nHouse after the giving of the authorization.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a138e46bd75822b60a842c3a730db9714199e8da4b3bc3dee21a776366bfc91c",
      "skos:note": "Conditional commencement of proposal implementation without compliance with subsection (3)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-6-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(4) Functions of Bureau",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where, in relation to a proposal to which subsection (3) is\napplicable, being a proposal for the collection of information\nrelating to businesses, the Minister considers it necessary to\ncommence implementation of the proposal at a time when it is not\npracticable to comply with subsection (3) the Minister may\nauthorize the implementation of the proposal without compliance\nwith that subsection but in such a case particulars of the nature of\nthe information to which the authorization relates shall be laid\nbefore each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days of that\nHouse after the giving of the authorization."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6(5) Functions of Bureau",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-6-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this section:\n\n(a) a reference to statistical purposes shall be read as including\npurposes in connexion with the collection, compilation,\nanalysis and dissemination of statistics; and\n\n(b) a reference to an official body shall be read as a reference to:\n\n(i) an Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act\n1999; or\n\n(ii) the holder of an office established for a public purpose\nby or under an Act or a law of an internal Territory; or\n\n(iii) a body corporate, or other body, established for a public\npurpose by or under an Act or a law of an internal\nTerritory other than such a body corporate, or other\nbody, that is declared by the regulations not to be an\nofficial body for the purposes of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of this section:\n\n(a) a reference to statistical purposes shall be read as including\npurposes in connexion with the collection, compilation,\nanalysis and dissemination of statistics; and\n\n(b) a reference to an official body shall be read as a reference to:\n\n(i) an Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act\n1999; or\n\n(ii) the holder of an office established for a public purpose\nby or under an Act or a law of an internal Territory; or\n\n(iii) a body corporate, or other body, established for a public\npurpose by or under an Act or a law of an internal\nTerritory other than such a body corporate, or other\nbody, that is declared by the regulations not to be an\nofficial body for the purposes of this Act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "774a7b0adab1f768ac977db1ba9fdfeab9c123a5d9cb2b38e8b34031d8196a0f",
      "skos:note": "Reference interpretation for statistical purposes and official bodies"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-6-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6(5) Functions of Bureau",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this section:\n\n(a) a reference to statistical purposes shall be read as including\npurposes in connexion with the collection, compilation,\nanalysis and dissemination of statistics; and\n\n(b) a reference to an official body shall be read as a reference to:\n\n(i) an Agency within the meaning of the Public Service Act\n1999; or\n\n(ii) the holder of an office established for a public purpose\nby or under an Act or a law of an internal Territory; or\n\n(iii) a body corporate, or other body, established for a public\npurpose by or under an Act or a law of an internal\nTerritory other than such a body corporate, or other\nbody, that is declared by the regulations not to be an\nofficial body for the purposes of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-6-ss-5-norm",
