    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-12-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12(4) Removal from office",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-12-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where such a statement has been laid before a House of the\nParliament, that House may, within 15 sitting days of that House\nafter the day on which the statement has been laid before it, by\nresolution, declare that the Statistician should be removed from\noffice and, if each House so passes such a resolution, the\nGovernor-General shall remove the Statistician from office.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where such a statement has been laid before a House of the\nParliament, that House may, within 15 sitting days of that House\nafter the day on which the statement has been laid before it, by\nresolution, declare that the Statistician should be removed from\noffice and, if each House so passes such a resolution, the\nGovernor-General shall remove the Statistician from office.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-12-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-12-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aae94d2574971235fa2d9d4f784edebb395258b63314db871326e3b18ed29b5f",
      "skos:note": "Parliament can declare the Statistician should be removed from office within 15 sitting days."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-12-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12(4) Removal from office",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where such a statement has been laid before a House of the\nParliament, that House may, within 15 sitting days of that House\nafter the day on which the statement has been laid before it, by\nresolution, declare that the Statistician should be removed from\noffice and, if each House so passes such a resolution, the\nGovernor-General shall remove the Statistician from office."
    },
