      },
      "dc:source": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the Statistician becomes bankrupt, applies to take the benefit of\nany law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors, compounds\nwith his or her creditors or makes an assignment of his or her\nremuneration for their benefit, the Governor-General shall remove\nthe Statistician from office.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) If the Statistician becomes bankrupt, applies to take the benefit of\nany law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors, compounds\nwith his or her creditors or makes an assignment of his or her\nremuneration for their benefit, the Governor-General shall remove\nthe Statistician from office.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-12-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-12-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "83d90b9441483554d2da8fbb6c5330b0d1434633b4dff82e83c8e195555d1969",
      "skos:note": "Removal from office if Statistician becomes bankrupt"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-12-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12(7) Removal from office",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(7) If the Statistician becomes bankrupt, applies to take the benefit of\nany law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors, compounds\nwith his or her creditors or makes an assignment of his or her\nremuneration for their benefit, the Governor-General shall remove\nthe Statistician from office."
