    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Functions of Council",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the Council are to advise the Minister and the\nStatistician in relation to:\n\n(a) the improvement, extension and co-ordination of statistical\nservices provided for public purposes in Australia;\n\n(b) annual and longer term priorities and programs of work that\nshould be adopted in relation to major aspects of the\nprovision of those statistical services; and\n\n(c) any other matters relating generally to those statistical\nservices.\n\n(2) Either the Minister or the Statistician, or both of them, may refer\nmatters of the kind referred to in subsection (1) to the Council for\nthe purpose of seeking the advice of the Council in relation to those\nmatters.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The functions of the Council are to advise the Minister and the\nStatistician in relation to:\n\n(a) the improvement, extension and co-ordination of statistical\nservices provided for public purposes in Australia;\n\n(b) annual and longer term priorities and programs of work that\nshould be adopted in relation to major aspects of the\nprovision of those statistical services; and\n\n(c) any other matters relating generally to those statistical\nservices.\n\n(2) Either the Minister or the Statistician, or both of them, may refer\nmatters of the kind referred to in subsection (1) to the Council for\nthe purpose of seeking the advice of the Council in relation to those\nmatters.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-18-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-18-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "276dd86a95d22a1d8ef5fc6f3073d040719433b5ff8700287f22b113f4cb4117"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Functions of Council",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The functions of the Council are to advise the Minister and the\nStatistician in relation to:\n\n(a) the improvement, extension and co-ordination of statistical\nservices provided for public purposes in Australia;\n\n(b) annual and longer term priorities and programs of work that\nshould be adopted in relation to major aspects of the\nprovision of those statistical services; and\n\n(c) any other matters relating generally to those statistical\nservices.\n\n(2) Either the Minister or the Statistician, or both of them, may refer\nmatters of the kind referred to in subsection (1) to the Council for\nthe purpose of seeking the advice of the Council in relation to those\nmatters."
    },
