          "@id": "concept:australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975-sec-19-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd74a676212099754ba743b10a4e23be8785159ebc49ef22d0d82d8cf76b0ea8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-bureau-of-statistics-act-1975#sec-19",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19 Membership of Council",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Council shall consist of:\n\n(a) the Chairperson;\n\n(b) the Statistician; and\n\n(c) such other members, being not less than 10 and not more\nthan 22 in number, as the Minister determines.\n\n(2) The Chairperson and the members referred to in paragraph (1)(c)\nshall be appointed by the Minister as part-time members, and shall\nhold office, subject to this Act:\n\n(a) in the case of the Chairperson—for a period of 5 years; and\n\n\nAustralian Statistics Advisory Council  Part III\n\nSection 20\n\nAustralian Bureau of Statistics Act 1975\nCompilation date: 3/5/19\nRegistered: 10/5/19\n\n(b) in the case of each other member—for such period, not\nexceeding 3 years, as is specified in his or her instrument of\nappointment;\nbut are eligible for re-appointment.\n\n(3) If the Premier of a State or the Chief Minister of the Australian\nCapital Territory or of the Northern Territory nominates a person\nfor appointment to the Council, the Minister shall appoint that\nperson as one of the members referred to in paragraph (1)(c) unless\nthe Council already includes a member appointed on the\nnomination of the Premier of that State or the Chief Minister of\nthat Territory, as the case may be."
    },
